\section{\uppercase{Prototype}}
\label{sec:experiments}

We coded the three mechanisms in Python and ran them on two families of $100$ randomized instances, seed $100$. Raw scores are uniform on $[0,100]$, the common bonus on $[0,15]$, $\delta=8$ unless stated, preferences over $V_i$ uniformly random, and each category enters $\T(i)$ independently with probability $0.45$ (a student drawing none is given one at random). Capacities are uniform on $q^o\le q^o_{\max}$, $q^t\le q^t_{\max}$, with $(|I|,|T|,q^o_{\max},q^t_{\max})=(200,6,30,15)$ and $(60,6,30,15)$, offering on average $47.99$ and $47.16$ reserve seats. The second family is the point: in the first, capacity falls well short of $|I|$ and the mechanisms cannot separate on coverage; the second inverts this, average total capacity $64.25$ against $|I|=60$. PA-ODR takes the admitted set by matroid greedy and then one min-cost assignment. Every property is checked against its definition.

