Several questions remain. The sharpest is whether A-STDA is strategy-proof: a positive answer would exhibit a score-feasible, capacity-preserving, strategy-proof mechanism, making the loss of Proposition~\ref{prop:paodr-notsp} a cost of reserve-completeness rather than of score-feasibility; a negative one would suggest an incentive counterpart to Proposition~\ref{prop:impossibility}. Neither our $210{,}000$-instance search nor Proposition~\ref{prop:spse-sp} settles it. Second, whether A-STDA satisfies Definition~\ref{def:nw} at a reserve category. Third, whether minimum de-reservation is computable efficiently for unbounded $|T|$, where we conjecture hardness, realizability resting on a Hall-type condition over all subsets of $T$; Cs\'aji and Sun \cite{CsSu26a} solve the nearest fixed-market problem in polynomial time, while overlapping types with per-type quotas are $\Sigma_2^{\mathrm{P}}$-complete \cite{CGH20a}. Fourth, whether routing is essential at all: one could apply the bonus and admit purely by adjusted score. Finally, the common bonus is deliberate: category-specific bonuses would break the property that an overlapping student is admissible for all her categories or none.

